Mailbox
├── when the contract is deployed
│   └── it should disable initializers
├── when reinitialize is called
│   ├── when caller is not DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE for reinitialize
│   │   └── it should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount(account, role)
│   └── when caller is DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE for reinitialize
│       ├── it should grant ADMIN_AUTHORITY_ROLE to caller
│       └── it should emit Reinitialized event
├── when _authorizeUpgrade is called
│   ├── when caller is not admin for _authorizeUpgrade
│   │   └── it should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount(account, role)
│   └── when caller is admin for _authorizeUpgrade
│       └── it should allow the upgrade
├── when getVersionComponents is called
│   └── it should return correct version numbers
├── when addModule is called
│   ├── when caller is not admin for addModule
│   │   └── it should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount(account, role)
│   ├── when moduleId is already set for addModule
│   │   └── it should revert with ModuleAddressForModuleIDAlreadySet
│   └── when conditions are met for addModule
│       ├── it should set the module address
│       └── it should grant MODULE_ROLE to the module
├── when removeModule is called
│   ├── when caller is not admin for removeModule
│   │   └── it should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount(account, role)
│   ├── when moduleId does not exist for removeModule
│   │   └── it should revert with ModuleAddressForModuleNotSet
│   ├── when module address mismatch for removeModule
│   │   └── it should revert with ModuleAddressMismatch
│   └── when conditions are met for removeModule
│       ├── it should remove the module
│       └── it should revoke MODULE_ROLE from the module
├── when updateModule is called
│   ├── when caller is not admin for updateModule
│   │   └── it should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount(account, role)
│   ├── when moduleId does not exist for updateModule
│   │   └── it should revert with ModuleAddressForModuleNotSet
│   ├── when old module address mismatch for updateModule
│   │   └── it should revert with ModuleAddressMismatch
│   └── when conditions are met for updateModule
│       ├── it should set the new module address
│       ├── it should revoke MODULE_ROLE from old module
│       ├── it should grant MODULE_ROLE to new module
│       └── it should emit ModuleUpdated event
├── when receiveMessage is called
│   ├── when caller is not trusted relayer for receiveMessage
│   │   └── it should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount(account, role)
│   ├── when chain ID is not Eclipse for receiveMessage
│   │   └── it should revert with NotFromEclipse
│   ├── when nonce is already used for receiveMessage
│   │   └── it should revert with NonceAlreadyReceived
│   ├── when module does not exist for receiveMessage
│   │   └── it should revert with ModuleDoesNotExist
│   ├── when module call reverts for receiveMessage
│   │   └── it should revert with ModuleCallReverted
│   └── when conditions are met for receiveMessage
│       ├── it should mark nonce as used
│       ├── it should call the module
│       └── it should emit MessageReceived event
├── when sendMessage is called
│   ├── when caller is not a module for sendMessage
│   │   └── it should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount(account, role)
│   ├── when chain ID is not Eclipse for sendMessage
│   │   └── it should revert with NotToEclipse
│   └── when conditions are met for sendMessage
│       ├── it should generate a unique nonce
│       └── it should emit MessageSent event
├── when generateUniqueNonce is called
│   ├── it should return a unique nonce
│   └── it should mark the nonce as used
├── when view functions are called
│   ├── when ethereumChainId is called
│   │   └── it should return the correct Ethereum chain ID
│   ├── when eclipseChainId is called
│   │   └── it should return the correct Eclipse chain ID
│   ├── when moduleById is called
│   │   └── it should return the correct module address
│   ├── when receiveNonce is called
│   │   └── it should return the correct nonce status
│   └── when sendNonces is called
│       └── it should return the correct nonce status
├── when testing reentrancy protection
│   ├── when receiveMessage is called recursively
│   │   └── it should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount(account, role)
│   └── when sendMessage is called recursively
│       └── it should revert
└── when testing edge cases
    ├── when using maximum uint64 values for nonces
    │   └── it should handle them correctly
    ├── when sending very long messages
    │   └── it should process them correctly
    ├── when sending empty messages
    │   └── it should handle them correctly
    └── when multiple modules interact
        └── it should maintain correct state
        